  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-05-31T19:52:16.512Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I, and many others, have best friends or partners that despite being in a private world, or being set to \"ask me\" would always, ALWAYS agree to have be allowed to come to me/us and that's what this is a request for, for the permission system to have a per-person override. perhaps on their user profile? Where you can set something like \"bypass requests\" and this person is ALWAYS allowed to join you, any time. No matter if you're in a friends+, a private, a invite+. but at the same time it would need to be limited to a number so people can't just put -everyone- on it, or even come up with a popup like \"checking this box will allow this person to join you at any time, risking your privacy. Only check this if you are absolutely sure you trust this person\" \n\nOr even perhaps a \n\n\"set as partner\" for one (or several) people that overrides the blue,green, orange,red status to say \"this person can join me, no matter what.\"",
